# Tests of the `cthreads` module; generated from tools/cthreads.dsl by tools/build.py. They run under
# `refined test`, where machine and system targets work in the JIT's own process.

mutexTest is test
mutexTest purpose "A plain mutex is taken, refused to a second try, and given back; a recursive one is taken twice by its holder; storage keeps a value; thrd_current is equal to itself"
mutexTest verifies lockMutex excludesOthers
mutexTest verifies keyValue keepsValues
mutexTest verifies currentThread knowsItself
mutexTest verifies timedLockMutex stopsAtDeadline
mutexTest verifies timedWaitCondition waitsUntilDeadline
mutexTest typeParameter none
mutexTest input none
mutexTest output none
mutexTest outputOwnedBy none
mutexTest raises none
mutexTest effect use machine.memory
mutexTest effect use system.calls
mutexTest uses memoryAccess
mutexTest uses systemCalls
mutexTest memoryHeap false
mutexTest async false
mutexTest maxRecursion none
mutexTest label begin loopKind none
mutexTest label begin within none
mutexTest let n40 Int64 40 immutable
mutexTest let int320 Int32 0 immutable
mutexTest let int321 Int32 1 immutable
mutexTest let eight Int64 8 immutable
mutexTest let sixteen Int64 16 immutable
mutexTest let one Int64 1 immutable
mutexTest let int324 Int32 4 immutable
mutexTest let n48 Int64 48 immutable
